            {
                "entry_id": "76639ad8-058e-3a6b-a771-a4ff609671be",
                "word": "physic",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6e76ec9c-4fc9-4b1d-a259-5df2d588cd2b",
                        "entry_id": "76639ad8-058e-3a6b-a771-a4ff609671be",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "physics"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d98df2d2-c013-398f-a8a2-0235a8433740",
                        "entry_id": "76639ad8-058e-3a6b-a771-a4ff609671be",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A medicine or drug, especially a cathartic or purgative."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d9f6695-a153-46d6-af5c-06c7a2955c83",
                                "sense_id": "d98df2d2-c013-398f-a8a2-0235a8433740",
                                "text": "Harke yee Lords, you ſee I haue giuen her Phiſicke, / And you muſt needs beſtovv her Funerall, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a205e545-1163-4403-a697-250faa84ce0a",
                                "sense_id": "d98df2d2-c013-398f-a8a2-0235a8433740",
                                "text": "I ſhould not thinke it ſtrange, for 'tis a phyſicke / That's bitter, to ſweet end."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5298edf6-9c8b-4086-b0c5-8b3f9a6218e3",
                                "sense_id": "d98df2d2-c013-398f-a8a2-0235a8433740",
                                "text": "Nor can thy shame give physic to my grief."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ba67ee5b-6c88-4065-a2d8-1c024016f7db",
                                "sense_id": "d98df2d2-c013-398f-a8a2-0235a8433740",
                                "text": "Learn before thou speak, and use physick or ever thou be sick."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "45ed672a-5387-36a9-bc09-8aa1630cde17",
                        "entry_id": "76639ad8-058e-3a6b-a771-a4ff609671be",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The art or profession of healing disease; medicine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c45c3430-95fa-4d4e-a933-8ec36487cd77",
                                "sense_id": "45ed672a-5387-36a9-bc09-8aa1630cde17",
                                "text": "...and thus draw out all the unwholesome Air and Stench, which does more harm than any Physick can repair."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b917740b-e505-3705-acc4-d5e90093bd84",
                        "entry_id": "76639ad8-058e-3a6b-a771-a4ff609671be",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Natural philosophy; physics."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0db983d-9b6d-4a75-88f9-ae83defda854",
                                "sense_id": "b917740b-e505-3705-acc4-d5e90093bd84",
                                "text": "When I left Mr. Bates, I went down to my Father; where, by the Aſſiſtance of him and my Uncle John, and ſome other Relations, I got forty Pounds, and a Promiſe of thirty Pounds a year to maintain me at Leyden: there I ſtudied Phyſick two years and ſeven months, knowing it would be uſeful in long Voyages."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7ed821b3-558e-3d0f-8579-f7b269f34d1e",
                        "entry_id": "76639ad8-058e-3a6b-a771-a4ff609671be",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A physician."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "obsolete",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e4540bb-0ea6-4296-af00-9a690eab9177",
                                "sense_id": "7ed821b3-558e-3d0f-8579-f7b269f34d1e",
                                "text": "Desire is death, which physic did except."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
